# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets redirects.
# One rule per line, destination must be relative. The http → https and
# www → apex redirects live in worker/index.js instead: this format can't
# express a scheme or a hostname change.

# One canonical URL for the homepage. The sitemap, the canonical tag and the
# og:url all say "https://vibresia.com/"; make the server agree.
/index.html  /  301

# There is deliberately no rule for /share here.
#
# /share is a directory (site/share/), so Cloudflare serves its index.html for
# both /share and /share/ — which is what the custom-vibescape share page wants,
# and what the built-in vibescapes sit beside. A rewrite would be the obvious way
# to spell it, but a rule's source matches on path *prefix*: "/share ->
# /share.html" also matches "/share.html" itself, so the rewrite lands on its
# own destination and 307s to itself forever. Files that genuinely exist
# (/share/ribbons, /share/manifest.json) win the match, which is why the bug
# looked like it only affected the bare page.